# DATE FACTORY

## Git

Work on `main`. Keep `legacy-v1` and `legacy-v2` as archive branches.

## Donor / archives

For `донор` / `legacy` / «взять из донора»:

- Legacy V1: read-only `../date_factory_legacy` (`legacy-v1`)
- Legacy V2: read-only `../date_factory_legacy_v2` (`legacy-v2`)

Treat both archives as read-only sources. Copy the required files together with their dependency closure into this repository and retarget references to local `res://` paths. The resulting game remains fully self-contained when the archive directories are absent. Bring old domain architecture into the current project only when the task explicitly requires that architecture.

## Current product

`main` is Date System Lab: 2D text dating core + Developer Room.

Canonical product documents:

- `docs/MASTER_GDD.md`
- `docs/DATE_SYSTEM_LAB.md`

## GameState

`GameState` хранит только изменяемое состояние конкретного прохождения.

Статические определения игрового контента — параметры девушек, предметов, локаций, Stage, цены, базовые характеристики и прочие definitions — хранятся отдельно от `GameState`.

`GameState` хранит ссылки/ID и изменяемый прогресс относительно этих definitions.

## Canon-driven implementation

Project each request onto the existing Date System Lab canon and current systems before implementation.

Use the existing mechanics and architecture as the implementation surface. Extend the established solution directly instead of creating a neighboring parallel mechanism.

For canon lookup, locate the sections relevant to the current feature by heading/search and keep the retrieved canon context focused on that feature.

## Docs vs code

Keep documentation and code synchronized.

- Task is absent from the canon → add the canonical description first, then implement it.
- Task already matches the canon → implement from the canon.
- Request, docs and current code disagree materially → report the conflict to the user and wait for the decision.

## Verification ownership

The user owns normal player-facing visual/play verification by default.

The agent performs implementation checks, parser/compiler checks and requested automated tests. Use `df-qa-worker`, gameplay automation, screenshots and autonomous visual exploration when the user explicitly requests QA.

## Playable, not merely compiled

Done means the normal player route works: enter, use, exit and save/load where the feature requires it.

A debug-only implementation is an intermediate state. Report `NOT READY` while the normal player loop for the requested feature is incomplete.

## Scenes / look

Godot version: 4.7.1, Forward Plus.

Date System Lab is a 2D Control UI using containers and anchors, readable at 1280×720 and 1920×1080.

Preserve stable scene ordering during targeted `.tscn` edits. After generating or structurally changing a scene, reopen it in Godot.

## Scope

Prioritize a working POC inside the existing dating-core architecture.

Build adjacent world/economy/story/3D systems when their dedicated block reaches implementation.

## Large implementation blocks

Use cohesive implementation phases and carry discoveries forward inside each phase.

Preferred phase order for a cross-system Date Factory feature:

1. content/domain model;
2. engine/runtime logic;
3. UI / Developer Room / Simulator;
4. regression tests and docs.

Use the batched verification schedule from `code-intelligence.mdc`.

## Subagents

When a subagent is Cursor Grok, use the latest Cursor Grok version available.

## GodotIQ

`code-intelligence.mdc` is the project-specific authority for tool ownership, GDScript workflow and verification frequency.

Use GodotIQ's MCP `serverUseInstructions` as the generic capability reference, specialized by the project routing above.

Keep `GODOTIQ_RULES.md` as an on-demand full reference. Read the exact relevant section when a specific scene, editor, runtime, spatial or GodotIQ-tool detail requires it.

The default Date Factory verification ownership above applies to play, screenshot and explore workflows.
